WEBVTT

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.240
That ball went a bit high.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.870
I'm keeping it within your reach.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.540
Takakane!

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.870
What is it?

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.080
I...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.960
I wish we could stay like this forever.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.550
Yeah...

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.810
I won't be able to come visit you for some time,

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.020
so please wait a while.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.660
Isn't that...?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.250
That's meaningless.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.210
I already know the contents of that letter based upon your hand movements.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.710
You're hard to pull a fast one over.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.590
Lady Juana, why are you writing the letters from the little girl

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.550
that come in for the Chancellor?

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.680
That is because...

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.940
Thanks.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.950
I've heard Balfetto is the central figure

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.910
behind strategizing for the battle against the Spanish Armada.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.990
You aren't participating, Neshinbara?

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.830
Judge. I have no idea what this might try to do.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.790
Then when will you return to your duties as clerk?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.960
Shakespeare gave me an earful.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.670
She said I'm slacking.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.590
The difference between us is too great.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.810
Do you remember this?

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.310
You wrote this in elementary school.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.060
I believe it was your debut book, Neshinbara.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.480
The plot was super straightforward.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.150
There were hidden bloodlines and rage induced bursts of power.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.530
And as the writer, you were too embarrassed to include more than a mere kiss.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.740
You don't have to mention everything, Asama!

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.370
Yeah, but Tori told me to.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.290
Aoi read this?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.710
Here's something else he said:

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.500
I don't know what Shakespeare wrote when she was a kid,

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.710
but Neshinbara's work has to be way crazier than hers.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.300
It's beyond saving when even I don't feel like defending it.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.020
Well then, the festival is now over.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:16.990
Everyone, I have just received information that Tres España's armada has left port.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.070
As mercenaries serving England,

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.910
our vessel will participate in this battle. Over.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.050
What is the meaning of this, Margot?!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.300
Why am I not allowed to fight?

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.680
If it's about my wings, look! I can move them again!

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.350
I can fly!

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.940
Malga, that isn't the issue.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.190
Then what? Is it because I'm <i>weak</i>?!

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.980
Am I useless without Weisse Frauen?!

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.110
Or is it because of my father?

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.820
Don't worry about me.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.490
Even if I were to die shielding you,

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.950
I'd be cool with it as long as you survived.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.870
I could do anything!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.750
After all, it'd all be for you, Margot!

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.710
You cowardly chicken!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.390
Wow!

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.610
What's your problem?

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.530
Listen. This is what you just said,

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.910
If I die, it's because of you, Naito.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.540
I got beaten to death,

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:52.040
but I did it for you and don't you ever forget it.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.840
You think sacrificing yourself is enough to stay with someone?

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.130
Aren't you taking love too lightly?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.130
Margot...

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.470
What is it, Malga?

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.850
Could you use my help?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.020
I don't think I need your help the way you are right now.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.230
Judge, you're right.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.440
If I depend on you, we won't be equals anymore...

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.520
We'd be over.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.820
Judge.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.030
Zwei Frauen means to stand side by side.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.820
Do you think we're always standing as equals?

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.870
Aren't we called Zwei Frauen

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.660
because that's what we try for?

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.750
Technohexen believe in their nicknames.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.580
Isn't that right?

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.090
Some moron punched me and I can't get up.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:40.920
Could you lend me a hand?

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:50.640
Is Tenzo around?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.560
No, I haven't seen him.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:57.770
Yeah? This just came in.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:00.780
Let's see...

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:04.530
This is...!

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:09.410
Listen, do something about this before Musashi sets sail.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:14.660
Sir Grac, you are truly of Far East origins?

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.670
Tes. I was one of the Ten Brave Amago Warriors, Yokomichi Hyogonosuke.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.880
I have my reasons for owing Queen Mary a debt of honor.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.420
Is that right?

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.180
What's the plan, kid?

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.850
It will be nearly impossible to sneak past all of them.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.810
It'll be okay.

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.230
And even if something should happen,

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.020
I am currently only responsible for myself.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.100
Now I see.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.940
Oh, the King asked us to pick up some black tea from this shop.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:46.570
Hmm, they might be closed for the night, Sir Tori.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.360
Whoa!

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.280
What was your big announcement?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.200
Don't try to wander off somewhere without telling us first.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.790
I... am going to confess how I feel to someone.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:07:59.500
Has he snapped?

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.540
He's snapped. Has he snapped?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.210
He must have snapped.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.340
He's totally snapped. He must have snapped.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.210
Could you tell me one thing?

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.130
Why are you gonna rescue that Mary girl?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.180
She has scarred me.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.310
So I am going to ask her if she could give me

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:17.850
an even deeper scar.

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.230
Are you seriously gonna tell her how ya feel?

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:24.690
Judge! In other words, I have fallen in love!

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.740
Oh, you fell in love?

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.860
Then there's no stopping you!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.490
Why are you going to save her?

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:30.870
What?

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.030
She wants to die.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:37.750
If I lose Master Mary, it would make me sad.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.580
Ninja is written as heart under blade.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.710
As such, ninja are told to suppress their emotions.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:51.760
But even so, the character for heart has not been removed from the character for ninja!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.020
So would it have saddened someone if I died

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.890
during my own near-execution?

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:58.810
Judge!

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:11.200
Then if we were to lose Master Mary,

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.490
would it sadden me as well?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.700
Judge, I'm sure of it.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.000
Have you reached your decision?

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.080
Judge.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.790
If you are going to conquer the world,

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:26.630
give me negative emotions and begin a happy life,

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:30.050
then I shall say this from a parallel stance.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.260
We are parallel.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:37.390
I shall save the world from the ultimate loss referred to as the apocalypse

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:42.810
and begin my happy life by not using the negative emotions given to me.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.400
That is my decision.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.440
Masazumi.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.150
Wh-What?! What did you just say?

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.740
It looks like we're going to war with England to save Mary.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:59.580
It would be all right if the representative duels began in 30 minutes, right?

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.580
We'll be sure to fight the Armada, too.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.750
Why you...!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.540
You randomly picked a fight with us last time,

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.550
so you won't run from our challenge, now will you?

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.380
Y-You fools!

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.930
You sure about this, Horizon?

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.970
Judge. I discern that was well done.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.560
So there you have it. Now get going, Tenzo.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.390
I shall accompany you.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:26.060
A knight cannot lower herself by serving as a mercenary.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.730
Besides, it allows me to show my gratitude to that hound.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.990
Then I'd better go as well.

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:36.490
I cannot draw my weapon against Tres España, as they are Catholic.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:40.040
I'll stay here to serve as a witness.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.000
It would stink if we didn't have someone declare when the battle is over.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.540
Lastly, let's bring...

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.880
I'll go.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:47.840
Sir Neshinbara?!

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:52.380
I'll fight Shakespeare and bring back her Armament of Deadly Sins.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:57.340
Oh, did you read your old masterpiece?

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.600
I sure did.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.850
I've always been a genius, haven't I?

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:02.470
Uh-huh!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.640
Please save Master Mary, kids!

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:09.320
Sir Milton, I have a small favor to ask of you.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.130
Well then, shall we head out?

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.780
In the end, I never got to see his face.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:58.700
Milton?

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:10.130
Isn't this...? But it can't be!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.990
See, I've been through a lot.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:44.240
So I don't much care for the concept that Elves are superior.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:51.750
Now then, didn't you say your dream was to someday help him?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.300
Then do so with all your might.

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:01.840
I'd be willing to support you and your lie if it's for that.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.310
Until the time I must part with the man I hold dear...

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.270
Until then...

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.560
From Inadequate HQ to everyone,

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:14.940
I hereby present Master Adele Balfetto,

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:18.650
speaking as our substitute captain. Over.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:22.280
Now then, allow me to explain the flow of the Spanish Armada battle.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.540
Basically, we'll intercept the Grande y Felicísima Armada,

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.330
but they will complete a full circle around England as they retreat,

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.790
during which time we will engage in combat four times.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:40.380
Won't they be quick to retreat so they don't take heavy losses?

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.680
Ammo isn't free, either.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.090
Indeed.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:47.430
I think they'll rush to finish their lap and retreat after we exchange broadsides.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:52.140
I was wondering, wouldn't it be best if we made some under-the-table deal?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.690
Since Musashi has been hired as a mercenary vessel,

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.520
we have to show results.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.490
Plus, the Testament Union will be watching us.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:03.240
If both countries act too friendly so they can retain national power,

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.450
they'll get punished for it.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:10.250
Lady Adele, it is just about time. Over.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.040
Judge!

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:16.790
Resuming acceleration.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.590
Upon passing under the Grande y Felicísima Armada,

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.590
we shall slip around behind them. Over.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.050
Everyone, please get things under way!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.240
What's this...?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.280
Reconfirming enemy location. Over.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.790
The armada split in two?!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.540
One part is headed toward England.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.670
A majority of ships have begun a retreat back to Tres España.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.710
The group of retreating battleships have not dropped speed.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:05.300
They are leaving the battlefield. Over.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.760
Why are they doing this...?

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.510
Please pull back.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.430
What are you doing?!

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:14.640
Who gave you orders to move the armada like this?!

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:19.940
Isn't he aboard that vessel?!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.570
Can you hear me?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:27.990
I am Tres España's Chancellor and President, Felipe Segundo.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.870
What is going on?!

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:32.240
Why did you have the Grande y Felicísima Armada pull back?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.460
They aren't pulling back.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:39.130
This old ship I'm on and the fleet that is about to pull up

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:41.920
are what compose the true Grande y Felicísima Armada.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.210
Take a look.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.340
I determine that they are the size of small fishing boats.

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:52.810
I suspect they were hiding in the waves. Over.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.140
Wh-What in the...?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.150
Are those the ships they used in Lepanto?

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.530
Yes. Indeed they are.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:09.160
I'm here!

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:10.780
I'm here, Admiral!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.370
I'm here to save you, just as I promised!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:13.740
Oh, you're our captain!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.040
Tes. Thank you for coming.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:19.630
Let's make this our final Falles.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.590
Let us hereby begin the Spanish Armada battle.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:28.680
We are going to put all of our might into sinking Musashi.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.800
But as reenacting history dictates,

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.560
my Grande y Felicísima Armada will be utterly destroyed.

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:36.060
But I want you to remember.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:43.070
Even if you destroy our armada... Tres España's naval powers, including the San Martin, will remain unscathed.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:48.030
You're using the remaining ships from Lepanto to represent the Grande y Felicísima Armada?!

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:51.490
I failed to protect my wife and child.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.790
So this is what I thought when I was appointed as Chancellor:

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:58.580
Ah, my dying grounds have already been laid out for me.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.710
I'm being told to give back by protecting something big at the end of my life.

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:07.170
I am neither a hero nor a king.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:10.590
I am merely a coward who wound up surviving.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:15.140
But isn't it okay for me to try and save Tres España?

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.470
Chancellor! What about me?!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:19.730
What about what I want?

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:21.440
I don't want to be left behind!

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.020
Mister!

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.730
Mister...?

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:31.610
I'm sorry. I'm sorry I lied.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:35.030
So... please don't leave me!

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:43.040
I am the girl he saved back then, Tachibana Gin.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.710
Since Tres España is a purist nation,

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.090
we have some who are oppressed.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:50.880
They are called Half Elves.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:51.550
Tes.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:59.390
Then what would you say if the girl he saved in that Elven village was a Half Elf?

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:04.350
What if she had been born from an act of infidelity and locked away?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:09.940
What if she couldn't trust the man who had saved her from those horrors and lied about herself?

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.570
What if she couldn't repay him for saving her without that lie?

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.330
And what if while she feels grateful for the position she has achieved through that lie,

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:21.160
but also feels utter remorse for telling that lie?

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.040
What should I do?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:31.170
I simply want to help him, even if just a little.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.340
That is all I desire and yet...

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:36.890
Juana...

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.850
How should I put this?

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.810
You don't have to pretend you're that girl.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.650
Commander of the retreating fleet!

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:49.780
Tes.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.820
Supposedly the girl I saved was a Half Elf.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:59.280
Juana here is lying in an attempt to stop a lug like me.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:03.910
Tes. Jua is an Elf. I guarantee it.

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:05.500
Thank you.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:11.130
Juana, you've become quite the lady.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:24.310
In hope that the Grande y Felicísima Armada is victorious,

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:25.230
prepare the salute!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:31.270
Fire!

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:39.660
Ether cannonballs and physical blessed cannonballs will hit in 15 seconds. Over.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:17.240
Isn't Musashi in a bind?

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:22.530
Yeah, that Chancellor Segundo is using a Rolling Wheel Formation on both sides.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:27.460
Thanks to that, they don't create any openings with loading times and can constantly attack.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:31.000
Doesn't that mean that Musashi can't counter-attack?

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.500
Tes. That is correct.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:39.260
We almost have them!

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.140
Keep pushing!

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.600
They analyzed our attack pattern?!

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:53.610
Judge! Gunner Crew, please break the enemy's formation!

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:58.110
Upon doing so, we will put an end to the Battle of Plymouth!

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.030
Commence fire!

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.790
Damn, they broke our firing line!

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:12.460
Sorry!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.670
The next volley's coming!

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.420
Don't let them escape! Combine your line of fire!

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.840
Advance and regroup with the Admiral!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.690
<i>I am a coward.</i>

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:35.480
<i>But it's okay for me to believe that I'm not the type of person</i>

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:37.780
<i>that wastes the courage given to him, isn't it?</i>

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.530
Everyone, follow me to our next battle station!

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:44.530
We shall hereby go through the Battle of Portland

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:47.160
and the Battle of Calais in that order.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.170
I'm being taken lightly, aren't I?

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.130
War of the Roses.

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:18.860
What is with this cheap, thriller-style Noh horror play turn of events?!

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:21.490
Good evening, Miss Honda!

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:24.070
Is this your doing, Lord Chancellor Hatton?!

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:27.740
Yes! Jumping to the deathly point, I need you to die!

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:37.590
So you've come, usurper to the king.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.010
Please put Macbeth to an end, Shakespeare.

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:43.760
I have somewhere to go after this.
